1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:10,140
Call to order the regular meeting of the Miami Special Utility Authority for today's date and time.

2
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:14,039
Item 2 is an invocation by Pastor of First Assembly of God.

3
00:00:14,359 --> 00:00:16,339
Raymond, is he, Mr. Frizzell, here?

4
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:19,079
Chief, would you do the honors?

5
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:29,000
Father God, I thank you for this day, and I thank you for each person that attended here.

6
00:00:29,739 --> 00:00:35,280
I thank you, Father, for the leadership that Dean provides and the direction that the council provides.

7
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:39,539
I pray, God, that you would watch over them, watch over their families.

8
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:43,240
I ask that you be with the city employees and protect us.

9
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:47,140
I ask that this meeting be guided in a way that's pleasing to you.

10
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:48,920
It's in Jesus' name I pray. Amen.

11
00:00:51,399 --> 00:00:52,799
Brian, would you do the point, please?

12
00:00:53,719 --> 00:00:57,719
I pledge allegiance to the flag of the United States of America

13
00:00:57,719 --> 00:01:00,539
and to the republic for which it stands,

14
00:01:00,539 --> 00:01:05,260
one nation under God, indivisible, with liberty and justice,

15
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:05,859
for all.

16
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:07,239
Thank you, Brian.

17
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:08,680
Thank you, Chief.

18
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:12,040
Item 4 is public input and unscheduled personal appearances.

19
00:01:12,159 --> 00:01:16,299
Anyone of the audience that wishes to address the authority on any agenda items?

20
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,599
There being none, Item 5 is consent agenda.

21
00:01:20,719 --> 00:01:25,640
Staff is recommending Items 6 through 11 for the consent agenda.

22
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:30,340
If there are no questions on any of those items, I'd entertain a motion.

23
00:01:30,659 --> 00:01:31,439
I must do it for the mayor.

24
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:32,299
And a second?

25
00:01:32,540 --> 00:01:32,819
Second.

26
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:35,359
Roll call, please.

27
00:01:35,359 --> 00:01:35,799
Johnson?

28
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:36,359
Aye.

29
00:01:36,659 --> 00:01:37,159
Weston?

30
00:01:37,159 --> 00:01:37,659
Aye.

31
00:01:37,659 --> 00:01:38,159
Winchester?

32
00:01:38,159 --> 00:01:38,659
Aye.

33
00:01:38,659 --> 00:01:39,159
Lewis?

34
00:01:39,159 --> 00:01:39,659
Aye.

35
00:01:39,659 --> 00:01:40,159
Schultz?

36
00:01:40,159 --> 00:01:40,659
Aye.

37
00:01:40,659 --> 00:01:41,959
Item 12 is new business.

38
00:01:41,959 --> 00:01:42,659
Any new business?

39
00:01:42,659 --> 00:01:43,159
Anyone?

40
00:01:45,159 --> 00:01:48,159
Item 13, staff reports in your packet, if available.

41
00:01:48,159 --> 00:01:50,159
And the staff's present if there are any questions.

42
00:01:52,159 --> 00:01:54,459
Item 14 is trustee community announcements.

43
00:01:54,459 --> 00:01:56,159
Anyone have any announcements?

44
00:01:57,659 --> 00:02:05,420
I had asked the utility department's billing staff recently to give me some examples of some

45
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:07,920
of their cut-off process that they go through.

46
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:13,919
We've had a couple of complaints about the amount of the fee that's charged for the cut-off

47
00:02:13,919 --> 00:02:15,919
and then to re-establish service.

48
00:02:15,919 --> 00:02:19,419
And so I asked them to give me some examples of that, which I have and have kind of looked

49
00:02:19,419 --> 00:02:20,419
at.

50
00:02:20,419 --> 00:02:24,919
I'm just letting you know at a future utility authority meeting, I may want to revisit that.

51
00:02:24,919 --> 00:02:28,419
We passed an ordinance a couple of years ago, and it's been in effect now for a couple of

52
00:02:28,419 --> 00:02:29,419
years.

53
00:02:29,419 --> 00:02:32,419
And I think some of it bears going back and looking at.

54
00:02:32,419 --> 00:02:33,419
So just to kind of...

55
00:02:33,419 --> 00:02:34,419
Actually, I think that's been in effect for last year.

56
00:02:34,419 --> 00:02:41,419
So it's probably just fun that we take a look and see how it's affecting it.

57
00:02:41,419 --> 00:02:46,419
So just a heads up, and I'll ask them to share the information that I have and kind of the

58
00:02:46,419 --> 00:02:49,419
general nature prior to that time.

59
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:50,419
Item 15 is adjournment.

60
00:02:50,419 --> 00:02:53,419
Do we have a motion to adjourn the SUA meeting?

61
00:02:53,419 --> 00:02:54,419
I'll make a motion.

62
00:02:54,419 --> 00:02:55,419
And a second, please.

63
00:02:55,419 --> 00:02:56,419
I'll second it.

64
00:02:56,419 --> 00:02:57,419
Roll call.

65
00:02:57,419 --> 00:02:58,419
Forrester?

66
00:02:58,419 --> 00:02:59,419
Aye.
